review_text:
When you think the police should really stop pestering the mafia and no matter what happens you back the Boss, you know you've got it bad. 
 Well, that was me, reading Ruthless People. Of course selling drugs, killing people etc. is forbidden/awful/amoral (take your pick) but you still can't stop cheering for team "Giovanni-Callahan". That's how gifted J.J. Mac Avoy is. 
 To make it short, you should absolutely read this book if you: 
 -love mob stories; 
 -get high on "out of this world" strong heroine kicking butts or any other anatomy parts like she is eating ice cream, even her gorgeous husband's butt. And kicking is when she is in an exceptionally good mood...; 
 -want to read about sub plots and secondary character's dark secrets; 
 -like to take cold showers (honestly, not what I like but a necessity) because you've just read violent hot sex scenes; 
 -want action, action and more action. 
 If you can't stand all or one of these above, pass your way. 
 I will now watch Amazon and Goodreads like a hawk to dive in the second book as soon as it's published and it can't come soon enough. Miss Mc Avoy, if you ever need reviewers or even beta readers for the second installment, my door is wide open (I can always dream).

I feel like I went into this book with too-high expectations without even knowing what it was about. But I heard that was the best way, so I went on ahead, happy knowing that it was going to be some post-apocolypic-ish type book. 
 I wish I hadn't even know that much, because that's not even what the story was about. I still really enjoyed the story and all the amazing characters. I was so proud of myself when I recognized a reference to the book The Passage and then got confirmation in the notes in the back of the book. HOW AWESOME. 
 I just kinda wish there was more of everything.. it feels like the book was a little too spread out and wasn't able to focus too much on any on character before it would zoom back in time or flash forward back to the future. I want a sequel though. ; n;

3.5 stars; 
 I forgot how much a enjoyed this series! Eibhear & Izzy were a long time coming. A compliment and a compliment is that like fantasy novels, there's a lot of characters and storylines so you're never bored but as a romance novel, all I want is Eibhear and Izzy please. Focus on the coupleeeeeeeeee ): But the adventure was fun. 
 (note: I have actually read the entire series as to date, despite not rating all the books on goodreads, it's because the ones I didn't rate were the books where I may or maynot have kinda skimmed through stuff and not entirely fully read it...sometimes it happens, maybe I'll go back to them sometime haha)
